<title>TURKEY: Turkey's 10th beet test shows 8.66 T sugar per ha.</title>
<headline>Turkey's 10th beet test shows 8.66 T sugar per ha.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of Turkey's 10th and last beet test for 1996/97, carried out on October 30, showed a sugar output of 8.66 tonnes per hectare, compared to 8.71 tonnes at the same point last year, Turkey's state sugar refineries Turkseker said.</p>
<p>It said average sugar content was 16.7 percent, down from 16.9 percent in the 10th test last year.  </p>
<p>Turkey holds beet tests at 15-day intervals. The 10th test was compiled with data from 18 plants throughout Turkey.</p>
<p>Details follow.</p>
<p>			     10th test 96   10th test 95   9th test 96</p>
<p>Sugar weight</p>
<p> per hectare (tonnes)     8.660	    8.710	    8.530</p>
<p>Average sugar</p>
<p> content (pct)	     16.7	     16.9	     16.3</p>
<p>Number of beets</p>
<p> per hectare		 78,580	   82,230	   77,420</p>
<p>Root weight</p>
<p> per hectare (tonnes)    51.890	   51.560	   52.380</p>
<p>Ratio of leaf</p>
<p>weight to beet weight</p>
<p> (leaf/beet)		  0.32	     0.35	     0.35</p>
<p>--Ercan Ersoy, Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
